.TH DANBY-COOPERATION 1
.SH NAME
danby-cooperation \- density-limited mutualism between two species
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/cooperation
.SH MODEL
X' = X(a-bX+cY);
Y' = Y(d-eY+fX).
.PP
Each population is self-limited but increases the other's per-capita growth.
Finite coexistence requires be>cf.  As cf approaches be, the analytic
equilibrium moves outward; when cf is at least be this simple model predicts
unbounded mutual amplification and the origin is marked instead.
.SH DISPLAY
The phase portrait exposes the nullcline intersection and the histories show
whether cooperation settles or grows beyond the selected display range.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set initial populations.  The six bottom tracks set
the two intrinsic growth rates, crowding strengths, and cross-species benefits.
Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/cooperation.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/cooperation.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-competition (1),
.IR numerics (2)
